# CONFIG_USB_CDNS3_PCI_WRAP: MUST stay off on Sky1. It has no explicit line in
# this defconfig, so olddefconfig took its Kconfig default (default USB_CDNS3)
# and made it BUILTIN when USB_CDNS3 went to =y above. Its PCI match table is
# PCI_VDEVICE(CDNS, 0x0100) -- and Sky1's own PCIe ROOT PORTS enumerate as
# 17cd:0100 ("Cadence Design Systems, Inc. CIX PCIe Root Port", four of them,
# confirmed with lspci -nn on cixmini). So the Cadence USB3 PCI wrapper binds to
# the SoC's PCIe bridges and dereferences NULL in cdns3_pci_probe:
#
#   Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0x108
#   Call trace: cdns3_pci_probe+0x12c/0x360 / local_pci_probe / pci_device_probe
#   CPU 7 PID 1 Comm swapper/0 -- Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal
#
# Measured on O6N with r236 at 1.2s into boot, six reboot loops on the serial
# console. The faulting instruction f9008680 is str x0,[x20,#0x108] with x20=0,
# which is exactly the reported fault address.
#
# Sky1's real USB is CDNSP over ACPI (cdns-usbssp CIXH2031:* / CIXH2030:*), not
# the PCI wrapper, so nothing is lost by turning it off. The comment further up
# already records that making USB_CDNS3 builtin did not change the USB symptom
# it was meant to fix, so the wrapper it dragged in was pure cost.
# CONFIG_USB_CDNS3_PCI_WRAP is not set
# CONFIG_USB_CDNS3_TI is not set
# CONFIG_USB_CDNS3_IMX is not set
